course: dictionary
lesson: 15895
title: Unlabelled
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Unlabelled» has three parts: un- means not, label is a sticker or note that tells you what something is, and -ed shows it describes a thing. So unlabelled means without a label.
explain: «The jar on the shelf was unlabelled, so nobody knew if it held sugar or salt.» The clue is that nobody knew what was inside. A jar with no sticker tells you nothing, so unlabelled means it has no label to say what it is.
explain: In science, a diagram or graph that is unlabelled is hard to understand, because nobody can tell what each part or axis shows. Always label your diagrams and axes.
explain: Safety comes first. Never drink, taste or touch anything from an unlabelled bottle, because it could be poison or bleach. If you find one, leave it alone and tell an adult.
fact: Unlabelled means without a label, or not named or marked.
fact: «Unlabelled» has two Ls in British English; American English spells it unlabeled.
fact: «An unlabelled diagram» has no names on its parts, so it does not explain anything.
fact: In science, an unlabelled graph loses marks, because the axes must show what they measure.
fact: Never drink or taste anything from an unlabelled bottle: it could be poison or bleach.
exercise: «The bottle on the bench was unlabelled.» What does unlabelled mean? | Painted red | *Without a label | Very heavy | Full of juice
exercise: «Never taste anything from an unlabelled bottle.» Why is this rule important? | *It could be poison or bleach | It is too small to drink from | It tastes nice | It is always full of sweets
exercise: Find and copy the word that means without a label. | science | *unlabelled | jar | bottle
test: Why does an unlabelled graph lose marks in science? | It is drawn in pencil | It has no axes at all | It is too colourful | *Its axes and parts do not say what they show
test: Jayden finds an unlabelled bottle under the sink. What should he do? | Put it in his school bag | Pour it into his cup | Taste a little to see what it is | *Leave it alone and tell an adult
exam: Which sentence uses unlabelled correctly? | *The bottle was unlabelled, so nobody knew what was inside | The unlabelled bottle had a sticker saying "Juice" | The unlabelled cat ran up the tree | Unlabelled is a fruit that grows on trees
